<title>HONG KONG: Chi Cheung 1996 net rises 22.1 percent.</title>
<headline>Chi Cheung 1996 net rises 22.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   40.0   vs 37.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0    vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    101.20 vs 82.85</p>
<p>    Turnover		     507.82 vs 419.34</p>
<p>    Company name		 Chi Cheung Investment Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 10-16</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 8</p>
<p>NOTE - Chi Cheung is a property and financial investment company.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 10 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of four cents) vs eight cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
